From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] graph access hook, gegl_node_blit_level(), level-aware caches

1. gegl_set_graph_access_func(): a function called, in the calling thread,
   on entry of the functions which change a graph (properties, links,
   children, operation, passthrough, proxies) or evaluate it
   (blit, blit_buffer, process, processors, bounding box, detect).  GIMP
   renders its projection in a thread of its own and uses it to keep the
   main thread away from the graph while a chunk is being rendered.

2. gegl_node_blit_level(): renders a rectangle at a given mipmap level,
   whether or not mipmap rendering is enabled in the configuration.

3. Node caches at a level greater than 0: results were written into the
   cache (gegl:cache copied level-0 tiles into it, in level coordinates),
   which polluted the full-resolution cache.  Now reduced-resolution
   results are never stored in a cache (gegl:cache passes its input
   through), and a cache whose level-0 contents cover the request is read
   downscaled, which is exact.

4. tile-backend-buffer: a damaged level-0 tile (an uninitialized empty
   tile, when the source was only rendered at a level > 0) is not shared
   (gegl_tile_dup() warned thousands of times per reduced-resolution
   render); the copy provides its own empty tile.

5. gegl:median-blur at a level greater than 0: it read and wrote level-0
   pixels at the coordinates of the level.  It now reads and writes at the
   level, with the radius scaled (used by drop shadow, glows).

---
diff --git a/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c b/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c
index 67e33a2..3bb221b 100644
--- a/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c
+++ b/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c
@@ -245,6 +245,17 @@ gegl_tile_backend_buffer_get_tile (GeglTileBackendBuffer *tile_backend_buffer,
           return NULL;
         }
 
+      /* ChopGimp: a damaged level-0 tile is an empty tile whose data was
+       * never initialized (the source was rendered at a mipmap level > 0
+       * only, see gegl_tile_handler_empty): let our own empty handler
+       * provide it, rather than sharing it (and warning about it).
+       */
+      if (z == 0 && src_tile->damage)
+        {
+          gegl_tile_unref (src_tile);
+          return NULL;
+        }
+
       tile = gegl_tile_dup (src_tile);
 
       gegl_tile_unref (src_tile);
